Rem ==================================================================
Rem regextest.shoddy — test program for machines/regex.shoddy
Rem
Rem Assert-driven, in the xmltest.shoddy / jsontest.shoddy pattern: it
Rem prints what it is doing and stops the run at the first assertion
Rem that fails, ending with ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED when it does not.
Rem
Rem EVERY EXPECTED VALUE HERE IS A KNOWN ANSWER, WORKED BY HAND. Not one
Rem was recorded from a run, because a recorded span proves what the
Rem implementation did and not what it should have done.
Rem
Rem THE CENTREPIECE IS THE DIFFERENTIAL GRID. This file carries a
Rem SECOND, INDEPENDENT MATCHER — a naive recursive backtracker over the
Rem same parsed tree, written for obviousness with no regard for speed.
Rem It is the oracle. A grid of hand-written patterns is run against a
Rem grid of hand-written subjects and the two matchers are asserted to
Rem agree on the span AND on every capture, in every cell. This is what
Rem property-based testing looks like in this tree: tst/alg.shoddy tests
Rem integrals by differentiating them back rather than by memorised
Rem forms, and this tests a matcher by a second matcher for the same
Rem reason.
Rem
Rem It works as an oracle only because R4.3 fixes LEFTMOST-FIRST
Rem semantics, which is exactly what a naive backtracker has. Under
Rem POSIX leftmost-longest the engine would have no independent grader
Rem at all. THE ENGINE THAT MUST NOT SHIP IS THE ONE THAT GRADES THE
Rem ENGINE THAT DOES.
Rem
Rem The oracle is depth-capped and iteration-capped, and BOTH CAPS ARE
Rem ASSERTED NEVER TO BE REACHED by the grid — an oracle that silently
Rem gives up is worse than none. Patterns whose repetition body can
Rem match empty are deliberately kept out of the grid, because a
Rem backtracker loops on them where the virtual machine's visited set
Rem does not; those are asserted against the machine alone, and against
Rem hand-worked answers.
Rem
Rem THERE IS NO "WHAT CANNOT BE TESTED HERE" PARAGRAPH, AND THAT IS A
Rem RESULT AND NOT AN OVERSIGHT. Every other machine suite in this tree
Rem carries one: Shoddy has no catchable errors, so the aborting half of
Rem each guard pair cannot be exercised without killing the run, and is
Rem verified by hand and named in the header instead. This file has none
Rem to name. regex.shoddy contains no Error, so every refusal it can
Rem produce is a VALUE this file asserts on both arms, and 100% of the
Rem failure surface is under test.
Rem
Rem That sentence is also an acceptance check, and it is greppable:
Rem
Rem     grep -c "Error(" machines/regex.shoddy      must be 0
Rem     grep -c "Chr("   machines/regex.shoddy      must be 0
Rem
Rem If either ever is not, this header is a lie and the paragraph has to
Rem come back. Neither grep is sufficient on its own — every read of a
Rem character in that machine is bounds-checked by its caller, and no
Rem grep can check that.
Rem
Rem LIST-VALUED RESULTS ARE NEVER COMPARED WITH =. A List compares by
Rem identity in this runtime, so two structurally identical lists are
Rem not equal and an assertion that says they are proves nothing.
Rem Everything list-valued here is compared with ToArray(...) =
Rem ToArray(...), which compares structurally, or element-wise by Nth.
Rem This is the trap most likely to produce a green suite that says
Rem nothing, and tst/neuraltest.shoddy is the precedent.
Rem
Rem CASE IS FOLDED BY THE MILL, so a Case binder named p shadows a Def
Rem named P for the todo of the body. Every helper here is named at
Rem least three letters long for that reason.
Rem
Rem Nothing here touches a file, a socket, a window, or the terminal
Rem beyond Print.
Rem
Rem Build (once): build.ps1 build
Rem Run:          bin\mill run tst\regextest.shoddy    (from the repo root)
Rem ==================================================================

Include "../machines/regex.shoddy"

Rem ---- reading a pattern, for a suite full of literal patterns --------
Rem With no aborting twin (and there is deliberately none — see D11), a
Rem suite of literal patterns would be a suite of Select Case. This is
Rem the one convenience, and it lives HERE rather than in the machine:
Rem a bad pattern in this file is a BROKEN TEST, and Assert says so with
Rem the pattern and the reason named, where Error would only say that
Rem the program died.

Def Reads(pat As String) As RxProg
    ReadsAs(pat, RxNoOpts())

Def ReadsAs(pat As String, how As RxOpts) As RxProg
    Select Case RxRead(pat, how)
        Case Ok(prg)
            prg
        Case Err(wy, ofs)
            AssertBad(pat, wy, ofs)
        Case Else
            AssertBad(pat, "RxRead ANSWERED NEITHER Ok NOR Err", 0)

Def AssertBad(pat As String, wy As String, ofs As Number) As RxProg
    Assert(False, "THE TEST'S OWN PATTERN " & pat & " DID NOT READ: " & wy & " AT " & Str(ofs))
    Reads("x")

Rem ---- the two halves of a refusal, read without a match at each call --

Def Why(pat As String) As String
    Select Case RxRead(pat, RxNoOpts())
        Case Err(wy, ofs)
            wy
        Case Else
            ""

Def Ats(pat As String) As Number
    Select Case RxRead(pat, RxNoOpts())
        Case Err(wy, ofs)
            ofs
        Case Else
            0 - 1

Rem Whether a refusal names the construct. Contains is seq.shoddy's, and
Rem this file does not include seq, so the test is Instr — which is a
Rem builtin and answers 0 for absent.
Def Names(pat As String, phrase As String) As Boolean
    Instr(Why(pat), phrase) > 0

Rem ---- reading a hit without a match at each call ---------------------
Rem A miss answers 0 for the start, which no real hit can, so a suite
Rem line can assert a start and a length as two numbers.

Def HitAt(opt As Option) As Number
    Select Case opt
        Case Some(hit)
            RxHitAt(hit)
        Case Else
            0

Def HitLen(opt As Option) As Number
    Select Case opt
        Case Some(hit)
            RxHitLen(hit)
        Case Else
            0 - 1

Def HitText(opt As Option) As String
    Select Case opt
        Case Some(hit)
            RxHitText(hit)
        Case Else
            ""

Def Missed(opt As Option) As Boolean
    Select Case opt
        Case Some(hit)
            False
        Case Else
            True

Rem A group as a printable answer, with unset and empty told apart —
Rem which is the whole point of R4.2 and would be invisible if both came
Rem back as "".
Def GrpOf(opt As Option, gn As Number) As String
    Select Case opt
        Case Some(hit)
            GrpShow(RxGroup(hit, gn))
        Case Else
            "<no match>"

Def GrpShow(opt As Option) As String
    Select Case opt
        Case Some(txt)
            "[" & txt & "]"
        Case Else
            "<unset>"

Rem ---- list-valued answers, compared structurally ---------------------
Rem Never with =. Starts and lengths are pulled out as Arrays Of Number
Rem so a whole RxFindAll can be asserted in one line.

Def Starts(hs As List Of RxHit) As Array Of Number
    ToArray(Map(hs, RxHitAt))

Def Lens(hs As List Of RxHit) As Array Of Number
    ToArray(Map(hs, RxHitLen))

Def Texts(hs As List Of RxHit) As Array Of String
    ToArray(Map(hs, RxHitText))

Rem ==================================================================
Rem THE ORACLE — a second, independent matcher
Rem
Rem A naive recursive backtracker over the SAME parsed tree the machine
Rem compiles, written for obviousness with no regard for speed. It is
Rem the thing regex.shoddy exists NOT to be, which is exactly what makes
Rem it a fair grader: it reaches leftmost-first semantics by construction
Rem — try the alternatives in written order, take as much as you can and
Rem give it back a character at a time — where the machine reaches the
Rem same answer by a completely different route.
Rem
Rem It matches with an explicit CONTINUATION LIST: the nodes still to be
Rem matched after this one. A group opens by writing its start slot and
Rem pushing a shut marker onto that list, which is how the end slot gets
Rem written at exactly the right moment on exactly the right path.
Rem
Rem Two caps, both asserted never to be reached by the grid:
Rem
Rem   * OMaxDepth bounds the recursion, because a backtracker that runs
Rem     away takes the run with it.
Rem   * An unbounded repetition is given a concrete ceiling of the
Rem     characters actually left, which is exact for any body that must
Rem     consume something and is what keeps a body that need not consume
Rem     from looping forever. Patterns of the second kind are kept OUT
Rem     of the grid and asserted against the machine alone.
Rem ==================================================================

Def OMaxDepth() As Number
    400

Type ONode = ONil | OLit(OLitC As Number) | OCls(OClsNeg As Boolean, OClsRs As List Of RxRange) | OAny | OBol | OEol | OWb(OWbNeg As Boolean) | OCat(OCatL As ONode, OCatR As ONode) | OAlt(OAltL As ONode, OAltR As ONode) | ORep(ORepB As ONode, ORepLo As Number, ORepHi As Number, ORepLz As Boolean) | OGrp(OGrpB As ONode, OGrpN As Number) | OShut(OShutN As Number)

Type OSt = OWin(OWEnd As Number, OWCaps As Array Of Number) | OLose | ODeep

Type OPat
    OPRoot As ONode
    OPCaps As Number

Rem The translation bakes folding exactly as the compiler does, so the
Rem two matchers are compared on the same dialect and not on two.

Def OOf(t As RxNode, how As RxOpts) As ONode
    Select Case t
        Case RxNil
            ONil()
        Case RxLit(lc)
            OLitOf(lc, how)
        Case RxCls(neg, rs)
            OClsOf(neg, rs, how)
        Case RxAny
            OAny()
        Case RxBol
            OBol()
        Case RxEol
            OEol()
        Case RxWb(nb)
            OWb(nb)
        Case RxCat(lf, rt)
            OCat(OOf(lf, how), OOf(rt, how))
        Case RxAlt(lf, rt)
            OAlt(OOf(lf, how), OOf(rt, how))
        Case RxRep(bd, lo, hi, lz)
            ORep(OOf(bd, how), lo, hi, lz)
        Case RxGrp(bd, gn)
            OGrp(OOf(bd, how), gn)
        Case Else
            ONil()

Def OLitOf(lc As Number, how As RxOpts) As ONode
    If RxFold(how) And RxHasCase(lc) Then
        OCls(False, RxCaseBoth(lc))
    Else
        OLit(lc)

Def OClsOf(neg As Boolean, rs As List Of RxRange, how As RxOpts) As ONode
    If RxFold(how) Then
        OCls(neg, RxFoldRanges(rs))
    Else
        OCls(neg, rs)

Def OPatOf(pat As String, how As RxOpts) As OPat
    Select Case RxPAlt(Codes(pat), Len(pat), 1, 0, 0, how)
        Case RxTook(nd, nx, ng)
            OPat(OOf(nd, how), ng)
        Case Else
            OPat(ONil(), 0)

Rem ---- the matcher ----------------------------------------------------

Def OM(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, t As ONode, k As Number, caps As Array Of Number, todo As List Of ONode, d As Number) As OSt
    If d > OMaxDepth() Then
        ODeep()
    Else
        OM2(cs, n, how, t, k, caps, todo, d)

Def OM2(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, t As ONode, k As Number, caps As Array Of Number, todo As List Of ONode, d As Number) As OSt
    Select Case t
        Case ONil
            OGo(cs, n, how, k, caps, todo, d)
        Case OLit(lc)
            OEat(cs, n, how, k, caps, todo, d, k <= n And RxUnitAt(cs, n, k) = lc)
        Case OCls(neg, rs)
            OEat(cs, n, how, k, caps, todo, d, k <= n And (RxInSet(RxUnitAt(cs, n, k), rs) <> neg))
        Case OAny
            OEat(cs, n, how, k, caps, todo, d, k <= n And (RxDotAll(how) Or RxUnitAt(cs, n, k) <> 10))
        Case OBol
            OHold(cs, n, how, k, caps, todo, d, RxIsBolAt(cs, n, k, RxMulti(how)))
        Case OEol
            OHold(cs, n, how, k, caps, todo, d, RxIsEolAt(cs, n, k, RxMulti(how)))
        Case OWb(nb)
            OHold(cs, n, how, k, caps, todo, d, RxIsWbAt(cs, n, k) <> nb)
        Case OCat(lf, rt)
            OM(cs, n, how, lf, k, caps, Prepend(rt, todo), d + 1)
        Case OAlt(lf, rt)
            OAltGo(cs, n, how, lf, rt, k, caps, todo, d)
        Case OGrp(bd, gn)
            OM(cs, n, how, bd, k, SetNth(caps, 2 * gn + 1, k), Prepend(OShut(gn), todo), d + 1)
        Case OShut(gn)
            OGo(cs, n, how, k, SetNth(caps, 2 * gn + 2, k), todo, d)
        Case ORep(bd, lo, hi, lz)
            ORepGo(cs, n, how, bd, lo, ORepCeil(n, k, lo, hi), lz, k, caps, todo, d)
        Case Else
            OLose()

Rem One character consumed, or the branch dies.
Def OEat(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, k As Number, caps As Array Of Number, todo As List Of ONode, d As Number, ate As Boolean) As OSt
    If ate Then
        OGo(cs, n, how, k + 1, caps, todo, d)
    Else
        OLose()

Rem An assertion consumes nothing.
Def OHold(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, k As Number, caps As Array Of Number, todo As List Of ONode, d As Number, held As Boolean) As OSt
    If held Then
        OGo(cs, n, how, k, caps, todo, d)
    Else
        OLose()

Def OGo(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, k As Number, caps As Array Of Number, todo As List Of ONode, d As Number) As OSt
    If IsEmpty(todo) Then
        OWin(k, caps)
    Else
        OM(cs, n, how, First(todo), k, caps, Rest(todo), d + 1)

Rem The left branch is tried first and the right only if it loses, which
Rem is leftmost-first spelled as control flow. A depth answer propagates
Rem rather than falling through, or a give-up would read as a refusal.
Def OAltGo(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, lf As ONode, rt As ONode, k As Number, caps As Array Of Number, todo As List Of ONode, d As Number) As OSt
    OAltGo2(cs, n, how, rt, k, caps, todo, d, OM(cs, n, how, lf, k, caps, todo, d + 1))

Def OAltGo2(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, rt As ONode, k As Number, caps As Array Of Number, todo As List Of ONode, d As Number, got As OSt) As OSt
    Select Case got
        Case OLose
            OM(cs, n, how, rt, k, caps, todo, d + 1)
        Case Else
            got

Rem An unbounded max becomes the characters actually left, never fewer
Rem than the minimum. Exact for a body that must consume something.
Def ORepCeil(n As Number, k As Number, lo As Number, hi As Number) As Number
    If hi = 0 - 1 Then
        Max(lo, n - k + 1)
    Else
        hi

Def ORepGo(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, bd As ONode, lo As Number, hiE As Number, lz As Boolean, k As Number, caps As Array Of Number, todo As List Of ONode, d As Number) As OSt
    If lo > 0 Then
        OM(cs, n, how, bd, k, caps, Prepend(ORep(bd, lo - 1, hiE - 1, lz), todo), d + 1)
    Else
        If hiE <= 0 Then
            OGo(cs, n, how, k, caps, todo, d)
        Else
            If lz Then
                ORepLess(cs, n, how, bd, hiE, lz, k, caps, todo, d)
            Else
                ORepMore(cs, n, how, bd, hiE, lz, k, caps, todo, d)

Rem Greedy: one more repetition first, the continuation only if that
Rem whole path loses.
Def ORepMore(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, bd As ONode, hiE As Number, lz As Boolean, k As Number, caps As Array Of Number, todo As List Of ONode, d As Number) As OSt
    ORepMore2(cs, n, how, k, caps, todo, d, OM(cs, n, how, bd, k, caps, Prepend(ORep(bd, 0, hiE - 1, lz), todo), d + 1))

Def ORepMore2(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, k As Number, caps As Array Of Number, todo As List Of ONode, d As Number, got As OSt) As OSt
    Select Case got
        Case OLose
            OGo(cs, n, how, k, caps, todo, d)
        Case Else
            got

Rem Lazy: the continuation first, one more repetition only if it loses.
Def ORepLess(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, bd As ONode, hiE As Number, lz As Boolean, k As Number, caps As Array Of Number, todo As List Of ONode, d As Number) As OSt
    ORepLess2(cs, n, how, bd, hiE, lz, k, caps, todo, d, OGo(cs, n, how, k, caps, todo, d))

Def ORepLess2(cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, bd As ONode, hiE As Number, lz As Boolean, k As Number, caps As Array Of Number, todo As List Of ONode, d As Number, got As OSt) As OSt
    Select Case got
        Case OLose
            OM(cs, n, how, bd, k, caps, Prepend(ORep(bd, 0, hiE - 1, lz), todo), d + 1)
        Case Else
            got

Rem ---- the leftmost search, and the two renderings compared -----------

Def OFind(op As OPat, subj As String, how As RxOpts) As OSt
    OFindGo(op, Codes(subj), Len(subj), how, 1)

Def OFindGo(op As OPat, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, k As Number) As OSt
    If k > n + 1 Then
        OLose()
    Else
        OFindGo2(op, cs, n, how, k, OM(cs, n, how, OPRoot(op), k, SetNth(Dim(2 * OPCaps(op) + 2, 0), 1, k), { }, 0))

Def OFindGo2(op As OPat, cs As Array Of Number, n As Number, how As RxOpts, k As Number, got As OSt) As OSt
    Select Case got
        Case OWin(en, cps)
            OWin(en, SetNth(cps, 2, en))
        Case ODeep
            ODeep()
        Case Else
            OFindGo(op, cs, n, how, k + 1)

Rem The span and every capture, as one line. Comparing renderings rather
Rem than values is deliberate: a disagreeing cell prints what each side
Rem said, which is the whole diagnostic.

Def VmShow(prg As RxProg, subj As String) As String
    Select Case RxFind(prg, subj)
        Case Some(hit)
            Str(RxHitAt(hit)) & ":" & Str(RxHitLen(hit)) & CapsShow(hit, 1, RxCount(prg))
        Case Else
            "-"

Def CapsShow(hit As RxHit, gn As Number, ncap As Number) As String
    If gn > ncap Then
        ""
    Else
        " " & GrpShow(RxGroup(hit, gn)) & CapsShow(hit, gn + 1, ncap)

Def OrcShow(op As OPat, subj As String, how As RxOpts) As String
    Select Case OFind(op, subj, how)
        Case OWin(en, cps)
            Str(Nth(cps, 1)) & ":" & Str(en - Nth(cps, 1)) & OCapsShow(subj, cps, 1, OPCaps(op))
        Case ODeep
            "<THE ORACLE GAVE UP>"
        Case Else
            "-"

Def OCapsShow(subj As String, cps As Array Of Number, gn As Number, ncap As Number) As String
    If gn > ncap Then
        ""
    Else
        " " & OCapShow(subj, Nth(cps, 2 * gn + 1), Nth(cps, 2 * gn + 2)) & OCapsShow(subj, cps, gn + 1, ncap)

Def OCapShow(subj As String, a As Number, b As Number) As String
    If a = 0 Or b = 0 Then
        "<unset>"
    Else
        "[" & Mid(subj, a, b - a) & "]"

Rem ---- the grid -------------------------------------------------------
Rem Sized so the whole suite stays well under a second. The patterns
Rem cover alternation nesting, quantifier nesting, classes, anchors,
Rem boundaries, lazy forms and counted repetition; the subjects cover
Rem the empty string, one character, and strings that match at the
Rem start, the end, the middle and not at all.
Rem
Rem NOT ONE PATTERN HERE HAS A REPETITION WHOSE BODY CAN MATCH EMPTY.
Rem A backtracker loops on those and the machine does not, so they are
Rem asserted against the machine alone, further down, against answers
Rem worked by hand. Keeping them out is what lets the oracle's caps be
Rem asserted never to be reached rather than merely hoped for.

Def GridPats() As List Of String
    { "a", "ab", "abc", "a|b", "a|ab", "ab|a", "a*", "a+", "a?",
      "a*b", "a+b", "a?b", "a*?b", "a+?b", ".", ".*", ".+", "a.*b",
      "a.*?b", "a.b", "[ab]", "[ab]+", "[^a]", "[^a]+", "[a-c]+",
      "\\d", "\\d+", "\\w+", "\\s", "\\W", "^a", "a$", "^a$", "\\ba\\b",
      "\\Ba", "(a)", "(a)(b)", "((a)b)", "(a|b)", "(a|b)+", "(ab)+",
      "(a|b)(c|d)", "x(a|b)?y", "(a?)b", "a{2}", "a{1,2}", "a{1,2}?",
      "a{2,}", "(ab|a)(b?)c", "[ab]{2,3}" }

Def GridSubjs() As List Of String
    { "", "a", "b", "ab", "ba", "aab", "abb", "abc", "xaby", "aaa",
      "bbb", "xyz", "a b", "a\nb", "cab", "abcabc", "aabbcc", "ab12",
      "  a", "a-b" }

Def GridGo(pats As List Of String, subs As List Of String, how As RxOpts, cells As Number) As Number
    If IsEmpty(pats) Then
        cells
    Else
        GridGo(Rest(pats), subs, how, GridPat(First(pats), subs, how, cells))

Def GridPat(pat As String, subs As List Of String, how As RxOpts, cells As Number) As Number
    GridPatGo(ReadsAs(pat, how), OPatOf(pat, how), pat, subs, how, cells)

Def GridPatGo(prg As RxProg, op As OPat, pat As String, subs As List Of String, how As RxOpts, cells As Number) As Number
    If IsEmpty(subs) Then
        cells
    Else
        GridPatGo(prg, op, pat, Rest(subs), how, cells + GridCell(prg, op, pat, First(subs), how))

Def GridCell(prg As RxProg, op As OPat, pat As String, subj As String, how As RxOpts) As Number
    Assert(Instr(OrcShow(op, subj, how), "GAVE UP") = 0, "THE ORACLE'S CAPS ARE NEVER REACHED — " & pat & " OVER " & Shown(subj))
    Assert(VmShow(prg, subj) = OrcShow(op, subj, how), "THE VM AND THE ORACLE AGREE ON " & pat & " OVER " & Shown(subj) & " — VM SAID " & VmShow(prg, subj) & ", ORACLE SAID " & OrcShow(op, subj, how))
    1

Rem A subject with its newlines made visible, so a failing cell names
Rem something a reader can find.
Def Shown(subj As String) As String
    RxReplace(Reads("\\n"), Quoted(subj), "\\n")

Def Quoted(subj As String) As String
    "'" & subj & "'"

Rem ==================================================================
Rem THE SUITE
Rem ==================================================================

Def Main()
    Print("=== regextest: machines/regex.shoddy ===")
    Print("")

    Print("--- parsing: every accepted form ---")
    Rem One line per row of the dialect table, on the ACCEPTING arm:
    Rem each form reads, compiles, and matches what it says it matches.
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("abc"), "xxabcyy"), "LITERAL CHARACTERS")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("a.c"), "abc") And Not RxTest(Reads("a.c"), "a\nc"), "DOT IS ANY CHARACTER EXCEPT A NEWLINE")
    Assert(RxTest(ReadsAs("a.c", RxOpts(False, True, False)), "a\nc"), "AND ANY CHARACTER AT ALL UNDER DOT-ALL")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("[abc]"), "zzbzz") And Not RxTest(Reads("[abc]"), "zzz"), "A CLASS")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("[a-z]"), "9m9") And Not RxTest(Reads("[a-z]"), "999"), "A RANGE")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("[^a-z]"), "ab9cd") And Not RxTest(Reads("[^a-z]"), "abcd"), "A NEGATED CLASS")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("[a-z0-9_]+"), "ok_9") And Not RxTest(Reads("[a-z0-9_]"), "-"), "SEVERAL RANGES AT ONCE")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("[]a]"), "]") And RxTest(Reads("[]a]"), "a"), "A CLOSING BRACKET FIRST IS A LITERAL ONE")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("[-a]"), "-") And RxTest(Reads("[a-]"), "-"), "A DASH FIRST OR LAST IS A LITERAL ONE")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("\\d"), "x7") And Not RxTest(Reads("\\d"), "xx"), "THE DIGIT CLASS")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("\\D"), "x7x") And Not RxTest(Reads("\\D"), "77"), "AND ITS NEGATION")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("\\w"), "-_-") And Not RxTest(Reads("\\w"), "---"), "THE WORD CLASS")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("\\W"), "a-a") And Not RxTest(Reads("\\W"), "aaa"), "AND ITS NEGATION")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("\\s"), "a b") And Not RxTest(Reads("\\s"), "ab"), "THE SPACE CLASS")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("\\S"), "  x  ") And Not RxTest(Reads("\\S"), "     "), "AND ITS NEGATION")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("a\\nb"), "a\nb") And RxTest(Reads("a\\tb"), "a\tb") And RxTest(Reads("a\\rb"), "a\rb"), "THE CONTROL ESCAPES")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("\\x41"), "xAx") And RxTest(Reads("\\x7A"), "z"), "A CODE UNIT BY TWO HEX DIGITS")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("a\\.b"), "a.b") And Not RxTest(Reads("a\\.b"), "axb"), "AN ESCAPED METACHARACTER IS LITERAL")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("\\{\\}\\[\\]\\(\\)\\*\\+\\?\\|\\^\\$\\-\\\\"), "{}[]()*+?|^$-\\"), "EVERY ONE OF THEM, IN ONE PATTERN")
    Assert(HitAt(RxFind(Reads("^ab"), "abab")) = 1 And Missed(RxFind(Reads("^b"), "ab")), "CARET IS THE START OF THE SUBJECT")
    Assert(HitAt(RxFind(Reads("ab$"), "abab")) = 3 And Missed(RxFind(Reads("a$"), "ab")), "DOLLAR IS THE END OF IT")
    Assert(RxTest(ReadsAs("^b", RxOpts(False, False, True)), "a\nb"), "AND UNDER MULTILINE THEY ARE THE ENDS OF A LINE")
    Assert(RxTest(ReadsAs("a$", RxOpts(False, False, True)), "a\nb"), "BOTH OF THEM")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("\\bcat\\b"), "a cat sat") And Not RxTest(Reads("\\bcat\\b"), "concatenate"), "A WORD BOUNDARY")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("\\Bcat"), "concat") And Not RxTest(Reads("\\Bcat"), "a cat"), "AND ITS NEGATION")
    Assert(RxCount(Reads("(a)(b)")) = 2 And RxCount(Reads("(?:a)(b)")) = 1, "A CAPTURING GROUP COUNTS AND A NON-CAPTURING ONE DOES NOT")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("(?:ab)+c"), "ababc"), "AND A NON-CAPTURING GROUP STILL GROUPS")
    Assert(RxTest(ReadsAs("(?i)abc", RxNoOpts()), "ABC"), "AN INLINE FLAG PREFIX")
    Assert(RxTest(ReadsAs("(?s)a.c", RxNoOpts()), "a\nc"), "ANY OF THE THREE")
    Assert(RxTest(ReadsAs("(?ims)a.c", RxNoOpts()), "A\nC"), "AND ALL THREE AT ONCE")
    Assert(HitText(RxFind(Reads("a|b"), "zzbzz")) = "b", "ALTERNATION")
    Assert(HitLen(RxFind(Reads("ab*"), "abbb")) = 4 And HitLen(RxFind(Reads("ab+"), "abbb")) = 4 And HitLen(RxFind(Reads("ab?"), "abbb")) = 2, "THE GREEDY QUANTIFIERS")
    Assert(HitLen(RxFind(Reads("ab*?"), "abbb")) = 1 And HitLen(RxFind(Reads("ab+?"), "abbb")) = 2 And HitLen(RxFind(Reads("ab??"), "abbb")) = 1, "AND THE LAZY ONES")
    Assert(HitLen(RxFind(Reads("a{3}"), "aaaaa")) = 3, "A COUNT")
    Assert(HitLen(RxFind(Reads("a{2,}"), "aaaaa")) = 5, "A MINIMUM")
    Assert(HitLen(RxFind(Reads("a{2,4}"), "aaaaa")) = 4, "A RANGE OF COUNTS, GREEDY")
    Assert(HitLen(RxFind(Reads("a{2,4}?"), "aaaaa")) = 2, "AND LAZY")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("(?:)"), "anything"), "THE EMPTY GROUP PARSES AND MATCHES NOTHING, ANYWHERE")

    Print("--- parsing: every refusal, by reason and offset ---")
    Rem Both arms of every refusal in the dialect: the reason NAMES the
    Rem construct, and the offset is the 1-based place it was written.
    Assert(Names("(a)\\1", "BACKREFERENCES") And Ats("(a)\\1") = 4, "BACKREFERENCES, BY NAME AND AT THE BACKSLASH")
    Assert(Names("\\k<n>", "NAMED BACKREFERENCES"), "AND NAMED ONES")
    Assert(Names("(?=a)", "LOOKAHEAD") And Ats("(?=a)") = 1, "LOOKAHEAD")
    Assert(Names("(?!a)", "NEGATIVE LOOKAHEAD"), "NEGATIVE LOOKAHEAD")
    Assert(Names("(?<=a)", "LOOKBEHIND") And Ats("(?<=a)") = 1, "LOOKBEHIND")
    Assert(Names("(?<!a)", "NEGATIVE LOOKBEHIND"), "NEGATIVE LOOKBEHIND")
    Assert(Names("(?<nm>a)", "NAMED GROUPS") And Names("(?P<nm>a)", "NAMED GROUPS") And Names("(?'nm'a)", "NAMED GROUPS"), "NAMED GROUPS, ALL THREE SPELLINGS")
    Assert(Names("(?>a)", "ATOMIC GROUPS"), "ATOMIC GROUPS")
    Assert(Names("a*+", "POSSESSIVE") And Ats("a*+") = 3, "POSSESSIVE QUANTIFIERS, AT THE PLUS")
    Assert(Names("(?(1)a)", "CONDITIONALS"), "CONDITIONALS")
    Assert(Names("(?R)", "RECURSION") And Names("(?1)", "RECURSION"), "RECURSION AND SUBROUTINE CALLS")
    Assert(Names("\\Aa", "^") And Names("a\\z", "$") And Names("a\\Z", "$") And Names("\\Ga", "MATCH ANCHOR"), "THE FOUR ANCHOR ESCAPES, EACH POINTED AT WHAT TO WRITE INSTEAD")
    Assert(Names("[[:alpha:]]", "POSIX") And Ats("[[:alpha:]]") = 2, "POSIX CLASSES, AT THE INNER BRACKET")
    Assert(Names("\\p{L}", "UNICODE PROPERTIES") And Names("\\P{L}", "UNICODE PROPERTIES"), "UNICODE PROPERTIES")
    Assert(Names("(?x)a", "x FLAG"), "THE EXTENDED FLAG")
    Assert(Names("\\Qa\\E", "QUOTING"), "\\Q AND \\E, POINTED AT RxQuote")
    Assert(Names("(a", "UNMATCHED (") And Ats("(a") = 1, "AN UNBALANCED PAREN, AT THE ONE THAT NEVER CLOSES")
    Assert(Names("a)", "UNMATCHED )") And Ats("a)") = 2, "AND THE OTHER DIRECTION, AT THE STRAY ONE")
    Assert(Names("[abc", "UNTERMINATED [") And Ats("[abc") = 1, "AN UNBALANCED BRACKET")
    Assert(Names("*a", "NOTHING TO REPEAT") And Ats("*a") = 1, "A QUANTIFIER WITH NOTHING TO REPEAT")
    Assert(Names("a**", "NOTHING TO REPEAT") And Ats("a**") = 3, "INCLUDING ONE AFTER ANOTHER QUANTIFIER")
    Assert(Names("[z-a]", "BACKWARDS") And Ats("[z-a]") = 3, "AN INVERTED RANGE, AT THE DASH")
    Assert(Names("a{2", "UNTERMINATED {") And Ats("a{2") = 2, "AN UNTERMINATED BRACE, AT THE BRACE")
    Assert(Names("a{3,2}", "BACKWARDS"), "AND A BACKWARDS COUNT")
    Assert(Names("a(?i)b", "ONLY ALLOWED AT THE START") And Ats("a(?i)b") = 2, "AN INLINE FLAG MID-PATTERN")
    Assert(Names("(?i:ab)", "SCOPED INLINE FLAGS"), "AND A SCOPED ONE, WHICH IS A DIFFERENT MISTAKE")
    Assert(Names("a\\", "MAY NOT END WITH A BACKSLASH"), "A TRAILING BACKSLASH")
    Assert(Names("\\q", "NOT AN ESCAPE THIS DIALECT KNOWS"), "AN ESCAPE THAT SPELLS NOTHING")
    Assert(Names("[\\b]", "WORD BOUNDARY"), "AND \\b INSIDE A CLASS, WHICH WOULD OTHERWISE MEAN TWO THINGS")
    Assert(Names("\\xZZ", "TWO HEX DIGITS"), "A SHORT HEX ESCAPE")
    Assert(Names("[a-\\d]", "FAR END OF A RANGE"), "A SHORTHAND AS THE END OF A RANGE")
    Assert(Names("a{3000}", "TOO MANY REPETITIONS") And Instr(Why("a{3000}"), "2000") > 0, "A COUNT PAST THE CAP, REFUSED AT PARSE TIME AND NAMING THE NUMBER")
    Assert(Names("(a{100}){100}", "TOO MANY REPETITIONS"), "AND A NESTED ONE, WHICH IS THE SHAPE THAT ACTUALLY BLOWS UP")
    Assert(Why("abc") = "" And Ats("abc") = 0 - 1, "AND A GOOD PATTERN REFUSES NOTHING")

    Print("--- the character domain ---")
    Rem ASCII folding, asserted IN THE NEGATIVE as well as the positive:
    Rem the negative half is the one that would otherwise be assumed.
    Assert(RxTest(ReadsAs("abc", RxFoldOpts()), "ABC") And RxTest(ReadsAs("ABC", RxFoldOpts()), "abc"), "FOLDING MATCHES A WITH a")
    Assert(RxTest(ReadsAs("[a-z]+", RxFoldOpts()), "ABC"), "AND CARRIES INTO A CLASS")
    Assert(Not RxTest(ReadsAs("[^a]", RxFoldOpts()), "A"), "AND INTO A NEGATED ONE, WHICH IS WHERE IT WOULD GO WRONG")
    Assert(Not RxTest(ReadsAs(FromCodes({ 196 }), RxFoldOpts()), FromCodes({ 228 })), "AND DOES NOT MATCH A-DIAERESIS WITH ITS LOWER CASE — THE FOLDING IS ASCII, EXACTLY")
    Assert(Not RxTest(ReadsAs("abc", RxNoOpts()), "ABC"), "AND WITHOUT THE OPTION CASE IS COMPARED EXACTLY")
    Rem A non-BMP character is TWO code units and the dot matches one.
    Let pair = FromCodes({ 55357, 56832 })
    Assert(Len(pair) = 2, "A NON-BMP CHARACTER IS TWO CODE UNITS")
    Assert(HitLen(RxFind(Reads("^..$"), pair)) = 2, "AND TWO DOTS MATCH IT WHOLE")
    Assert(HitLen(RxFind(Reads("."), pair)) = 1, "AND ONE DOT MATCHES ONE OF THEM")
    Rem NUL. This is the assertion that would have to be deleted if the
    Rem runtime ever went back on FromCodes.
    Let withNul = FromCodes({ 65, 0, 66 })
    Assert(Len(withNul) = 3, "A STRING CAN CARRY A NUL, BECAUSE FromCodes CAN BUILD ONE")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("A\\x00B"), withNul), "AND \\x00 MATCHES IT")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("A\\0B"), withNul), "AND SO DOES \\0")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("A[\\0]B"), withNul), "AND SO DOES A NUL INSIDE A CLASS")
    Assert(Length(RxFindAll(Reads("\\0"), withNul)) = 1, "AND RxFindAll OF \\0 OVER IT FINDS EXACTLY ONE")
    Assert(Not RxTest(Reads("A\\0B"), "AB"), "AND A NUL IS NOT NOTHING — AB IS NOT A NUL B")

    Print("--- leftmost-first ---")
    Assert(HitAt(RxFind(Reads("a|ab"), "abc")) = 1 And HitLen(RxFind(Reads("a|ab"), "abc")) = 1, "a|ab AGAINST abc MATCHES a — THIS IS PERL AND NOT POSIX")
    Assert(HitLen(RxFind(Reads("ab|a"), "abc")) = 2, "AND ab|a AGAINST THE SAME MATCHES ab, BECAUSE THE LEFT BRANCH IS PREFERRED")
    Assert(HitLen(RxFind(Reads("a.*b"), "axbxb")) = 5 And HitLen(RxFind(Reads("a.*?b"), "axbxb")) = 3, "GREEDY TAKES ALL FIVE AND LAZY TAKES THREE")
    Assert(HitAt(RxFind(Reads("b"), "abab")) = 2, "AND THE MATCH IS AT THE SMALLEST OFFSET AT WHICH ANY MATCH EXISTS")
    Assert(HitLen(RxFind(Reads("(?:a|ab)(?:c|bcd)"), "abcd")) = 4, "OUTSIDE-IN: THE FIRST GROUP GIVES GROUND SO THE SECOND CAN MATCH")

    Print("--- captures ---")
    Rem UNSET IS NOT EMPTY, and the type is what keeps them apart.
    Assert(GrpOf(RxFind(Reads("(a)|(b)"), "b"), 1) = "<unset>", "A GROUP THAT DID NOT PARTICIPATE IS UNSET")
    Assert(GrpOf(RxFind(Reads("(a)|(b)"), "b"), 2) = "[b]", "AND THE ONE THAT DID IS GOT, CARRYING ITS TEXT")
    Assert(GrpOf(RxFind(Reads("(a?)"), ""), 1) = "[]", "AND A GROUP THAT MATCHED NOTHING IS GOT, CARRYING NOTHING")
    Assert(GrpOf(RxFind(Reads("(a)"), "a"), 2) = "<unset>", "A GROUP THAT DOES NOT EXIST IS ALSO NONE — RxCount IS HOW THE TWO ARE TOLD APART")
    Assert(RxCount(Reads("(a)|(b)")) = 2, "AND RxCount ANSWERS HOW MANY EXIST")
    Rem ARITY: exactly RxCount entries, even when one cannot participate.
    Assert(CapCount(RxFind(Reads("(a)(b)|(c)"), "ab")) = 3 And RxCount(Reads("(a)(b)|(c)")) = 3, "A HIT'S CAPTURE LIST HAS EXACTLY RxCount ENTRIES, NEVER A SHORT ONE")
    Assert(GrpOf(RxFind(Reads("(a)(b)|(c)"), "ab"), 3) = "<unset>", "AND THE ONE THAT COULD NOT PARTICIPATE IS THE UNSET ONE")
    Rem NUMBERED BY OPENING PAREN, LEFT TO RIGHT.
    Assert(GrpOf(RxFind(Reads("((a)(b))"), "ab"), 1) = "[ab]", "GROUPS ARE NUMBERED BY OPENING PAREN: THE OUTER ONE IS 1")
    Assert(GrpOf(RxFind(Reads("((a)(b))"), "ab"), 2) = "[a]" And GrpOf(RxFind(Reads("((a)(b))"), "ab"), 3) = "[b]", "AND THE INNER TWO ARE 2 AND 3, IN WRITTEN ORDER")
    Rem A counted repetition duplicates its body's saves, so the LAST
    Rem iteration wins. That is what every other engine does, and it is
    Rem stated because the duplicated saves otherwise read as a bug.
    Assert(GrpOf(RxFind(Reads("(?:(\\w)){3}"), "abc"), 1) = "[c]", "IN A COUNTED REPETITION THE LAST ITERATION'S CAPTURE WINS")
    Assert(GrpOf(RxFind(Reads("(?:(\\w))+"), "abc"), 1) = "[c]", "AND THE SAME IN AN UNBOUNDED ONE")
    Assert(RxSource(Reads("a(b)c")) = "a(b)c", "AND A PROGRAM REMEMBERS THE PATTERN IT WAS READ FROM")

    Print("--- the empty-match rule ---")
    Rem THE WORKED TABLE, WHICH IS THE ONE RESULT CALLERS FIND
    Rem SURPRISING AND THE ONE AN IMPLEMENTATION GETS WRONG SILENTLY.
    Rem
    Rem   search at 1: "" (the b is not an a), length 0, next is 2
    Rem   search at 2: "aa", length 2, ending at 3, next is 4
    Rem   search at 4: "" at Len(s) + 1, past the end, next is 5, stop
    Assert(Length(RxFindAll(Reads("a*"), "baa")) = 3, "RxFindAll OF a* OVER baa IS EXACTLY THREE HITS")
    Assert(Starts(RxFindAll(Reads("a*"), "baa")) = ToArray({ 1, 2, 4 }), "AT 1, 2 AND 4")
    Assert(Lens(RxFindAll(Reads("a*"), "baa")) = ToArray({ 0, 2, 0 }), "OF LENGTHS 0, 2 AND 0")
    Assert(Length(RxFindAll(Reads("(?:)"), "abc")) = 4, "AND A PATTERN THAT ONLY EVER MATCHES EMPTY GIVES n + 1 HITS OVER A SUBJECT OF LENGTH n")
    Assert(Length(RxFindAll(Reads("x?"), "")) = 1, "INCLUDING ONE HIT OVER THE EMPTY SUBJECT")
    Assert(Starts(RxFindAll(Reads("ab"), "ababab")) = ToArray({ 1, 3, 5 }), "AND MATCHES OF LENGTH ARE NON-OVERLAPPING")
    Assert(Starts(RxFindAll(Reads("aa"), "aaaa")) = ToArray({ 1, 3 }), "WHICH IS WHY aa OVER aaaa IS TWO AND NOT THREE")

    Print("--- out of range, and not aborting ---")
    Rem A start below 1 is clamped, a fractional one floored, and one
    Rem past the end answers None. Each is the documented value, and the
    Rem suite reaching the next line is half the assertion.
    Assert(HitAt(RxFindFrom(Reads("a"), "xax", 0)) = 2, "A SEARCH START OF 0 IS CLAMPED TO 1")
    Assert(HitAt(RxFindFrom(Reads("a"), "xax", 0 - 5)) = 2, "AND SO IS ONE OF -5")
    Assert(HitAt(RxFindFrom(Reads("a"), "xax", 2.7)) = 2, "A FRACTIONAL START IS FLOORED")
    Assert(Missed(RxFindFrom(Reads("a"), "xax", 3 + 99)), "AND ONE PAST THE END ANSWERS None — NOTHING STARTS THERE")
    Assert(Missed(RxFindFrom(Reads("a"), "xax", 3)), "A SEARCH FROM 3 DOES NOT FIND THE a AT 2")
    Assert(HitAt(RxMatchAt(Reads("a"), "xax", 2)) = 2 And Missed(RxMatchAt(Reads("a"), "xax", 1)), "AND RxMatchAt IS ANCHORED AT EXACTLY ONE OFFSET")
    Assert(Missed(RxFind(Reads("a"), "")), "A MISS OVER THE EMPTY SUBJECT IS None AND NOT AN ABORT")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("^$"), ""), "AND THE EMPTY SUBJECT IS BOTH THE START AND THE END")
    Assert(3 + 4 = 7, "AND THE SUITE IS STILL RUNNING, WHICH IS THE OTHER HALF OF EVERY LINE ABOVE")

    Print("--- rewriting ---")
    Assert(RxReplace(Reads("[aeiou]"), "banana", "-") = "b-n-n-", "EVERY MATCH REPLACED")
    Assert(RxReplaceFirst(Reads("[aeiou]"), "banana", "-") = "b-nana", "AND ONLY THE FIRST, WHERE THAT IS ASKED FOR")
    Assert(RxReplace(Reads("x"), "banana", "-") = "banana", "AND A PATTERN THAT NEVER MATCHES CHANGES NOTHING")
    Assert(RxReplace(Reads("(\\w+)@(\\w+)"), "me@here", "$2/$1") = "here/me", "A TEMPLATE READS ITS GROUPS")
    Assert(RxReplace(Reads("\\w+@\\w+"), "me@here", "<$0>") = "<me@here>", "$0 IS THE WHOLE MATCH")
    Assert(RxReplace(Reads("b"), "ab", "$$") = "a$", "$$ IS A LITERAL DOLLAR")
    Assert(RxReplace(Reads("b"), "ab", "$") = "a$", "AND A LONE $ IS ONE TOO")
    Assert(RxReplace(Reads("b"), "ab", "$x") = "a$x", "AS IS A $ IN FRONT OF ANYTHING THAT IS NOT A DIGIT")
    Assert(RxReplace(Reads("(a)"), "a", "[$7]") = "[]", "A REFERENCE TO A GROUP THAT DOES NOT EXIST EXPANDS TO NOTHING")
    Assert(RxReplace(Reads("(a)|(b)"), "b", "[$1]") = "[]", "AND SO DOES ONE TO A GROUP THAT DID NOT PARTICIPATE")
    Assert(RxReplace(Reads("a*"), "baa", "-") = "-b--", "AND THE EMPTY-MATCH RULE IS THE SAME ONE RxFindAll USES")
    Assert(RxReplaceWith(Reads("[a-z]+"), "ab CD ef", Fn(hit) => Upper(RxHitText(hit))) = "AB CD EF", "A QUOTATION PER HIT IS THE ESCAPE HATCH A TEMPLATE CANNOT BE")
    Rem SPLIT: the pieces between matches, leading and trailing empties
    Rem kept, and capturing groups NOT emitted into the result.
    Assert(ToArray(RxSplit(Reads("abc"), "abc")) = ToArray({ "", "" }), "A PATTERN MATCHING THE WHOLE SUBJECT GIVES TWO EMPTY PIECES")
    Assert(ToArray(RxSplit(Reads(","), "a,b,c")) = ToArray({ "a", "b", "c" }), "AND AN ORDINARY SPLIT GIVES THE PIECES")
    Assert(ToArray(RxSplit(Reads(",\\s*"), "a, b,c")) = ToArray({ "a", "b", "c" }), "ON A PATTERN, WHICH IS THREE PASSES WITH A LITERAL SEPARATOR")
    Assert(ToArray(RxSplit(Reads("(,)"), "a,b")) = ToArray({ "a", "b" }), "A CAPTURING GROUP DOES NOT PUT ITS SEPARATOR INTO THE RESULT")
    Assert(ToArray(RxSplit(Reads(","), ",a,")) = ToArray({ "", "a", "" }), "AND LEADING AND TRAILING EMPTY PIECES ARE KEPT")
    Assert(ToArray(RxSplit(Reads("x"), "abc")) = ToArray({ "abc" }), "A PATTERN THAT NEVER MATCHES GIVES THE WHOLE SUBJECT BACK, IN ONE PIECE")
    Rem QUOTE: escaped so it matches itself and nothing else.
    Assert(RxQuote("a.b*c") = "a\\.b\\*c", "RxQuote ESCAPES THE METACHARACTERS")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads(RxQuote("a.b*c")), "a.b*c") And Not RxTest(Reads(RxQuote("a.b*c")), "axbbbc"), "AND WHAT IT ANSWERS MATCHES ITSELF AND NOT WHAT IT LOOKED LIKE")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads(RxQuote(withNul)), withNul), "INCLUDING A SUBJECT WITH A NUL IN IT")
    Assert(Why(RxQuote("[]()\\{}*+?|^$-.")) = "", "AND EVERY METACHARACTER AT ONCE STILL READS")

    Print("--- the differential grid: the VM against a backtracking oracle ---")
    Rem THE ENGINE THAT MUST NOT SHIP IS THE ONE THAT GRADES THE ENGINE
    Rem THAT DOES. Both matchers walk the same parsed tree and must agree
    Rem on the span and on every capture, in every cell.
    Let plainCells = GridGo(GridPats(), GridSubjs(), RxNoOpts(), 0)
    Assert(plainCells = Length(GridPats()) * Length(GridSubjs()), "EVERY CELL OF THE GRID WAS VISITED")
    Print("  " & Str(plainCells) & " cells agreed, span and every capture")
    Let foldCells = GridGo(GridPats(), GridSubjs(), RxFoldOpts(), 0)
    Assert(foldCells = plainCells, "AND THE WHOLE GRID AGAIN UNDER CASE FOLDING")
    Print("  " & Str(foldCells) & " more under folding, on the same tree compiled two ways")

    Print("--- it always returns ---")
    Rem The witnesses that hang a backtracker. REACHING THE NEXT LINE IS
    Rem THE ASSERTION — no timing is asserted anywhere, because a
    Rem wall-clock number in a suite is a flaky test on someone else's
    Rem machine.
    Assert(Not RxTest(Reads("(a|a)*b"), Runs("a", 30)), "(a|a)*b OVER THIRTY a's ANSWERS")
    Assert(Not RxTest(Reads("(a*)*b"), Runs("a", 30)), "(a*)*b OVER THIRTY a's ANSWERS")
    Assert(Not RxTest(Reads("(a+)+b"), Runs("a", 30)), "(a+)+b OVER THIRTY a's ANSWERS")
    Assert(Not RxTest(Reads("a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?a?aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"), Runs("a", 19)), "AND THE a? TIMES n, a TIMES n WITNESS ANSWERS TOO")
    Assert(RxTest(Reads("(a*)*"), Runs("a", 30)), "AND A STAR OVER A STAR STILL MATCHES WHAT IT SHOULD — THE VISITED SET CUTS THE LOOP, IT DOES NOT CUT THE ANSWER")
    Assert(Length(RxFindAll(Reads("(a*)*"), "aa")) = 2, "INCLUDING UNDER THE EMPTY-MATCH RULE")
    Assert(3 + 4 = 7, "AND THE SUITE IS STILL RUNNING")

    Print("--- the compiled program ---")
    Rem RxDisasm is how the docs page shows what "compiled to a program"
    Rem means, and how a disagreeing grid cell gets diagnosed.
    Assert(Length(RxDisasm(Reads("a"))) = 4, "save, char, save, match IS FOUR INSTRUCTIONS")
    Assert(Instr(Nth(RxDisasm(Reads("a")), 2), "CHAR") > 0, "AND THE SECOND ONE IS THE CHARACTER")
    Assert(Instr(Nth(RxDisasm(Reads("a")), 4), "MATCH") > 0, "AND THE LAST IS THE MATCH")
    Assert(Length(RxDisasm(Reads("a|b"))) = 7, "AN ALTERNATION ADDS A SPLIT AND A JUMP")
    Assert(Instr(Nth(RxDisasm(Reads("a|b")), 2), "SPLIT") > 0, "WITH THE SPLIT IN FRONT")
    Assert(Length(RxDisasm(Reads("a{4}"))) = 7, "AND A COUNTED REPETITION COMPILES BY DUPLICATION — FOUR COPIES AND THE WRAPPER")
    Assert(Length(RxDisasm(Reads("(?:)"))) = 3, "WHILE THE EMPTY GROUP COMPILES TO NOTHING AT ALL")
    Assert(RxCount(Reads("((a)(b))")) = 3 And RxCount(Reads("(?:a)")) = 0 And RxCount(Reads("a")) = 0, "AND RxCount COUNTS OPENING CAPTURING PARENS AND NOTHING ELSE")

    Print("")
    Print("ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED")

Rem ---- two more file-local helpers ------------------------------------

Def CapCount(opt As Option) As Number
    Select Case opt
        Case Some(hit)
            Length(RxHitCaps(hit))
        Case Else
            0 - 1

Rem n copies of s, built without str.shoddy's StrRep, which this file
Rem does not include.
Def Runs(s As String, n As Number) As String
    If n <= 0 Then
        ""
    Else
        s & Runs(s, n - 1)
